# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/004_predefined_macros.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness, no Cargo and no Rust toolchain: render the
# three command templates below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level,
# the source path, the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively
# executing target, that target's emulator otherwise).

program            = 004_predefined_macros
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Predefined macros asserted only as normalized relations: the standard conformance and version macros, the source-position macros, architecture-macro self-consistency, and the tie between the preprocessor's view of the target and the code generator's pointer width
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, and the argument below is the human
half of that guarantee; the two reference-compiler gates named at the end are the machine half.

TRANSLATION-TIME ARITHMETIC. Every controlling expression in this source either tests a macro with
`defined`, compares one against a small constant, or sums four operands each of which is 0 or 1 by
construction. The preprocessor evaluates such expressions in the widest integer type available to
it, so no operand and no intermediate result can approach an overflow. No shift, division or modulo
operator appears in any controlling expression, so no shift count can be out of range and no
division by zero is reachable. An identifier that survives macro replacement in a preprocessor
conditional is replaced by zero rather than diagnosed, and every conditional here is written so that
outcome is a defined 0 rather than an error.

RUN-TIME CODE. The only function besides `main` is `slen`, which walks a string literal from index 0
and stops at its terminating null byte. No pointer is formed past the end of an object, none is
dereferenced outside one, and no string literal is modified. There is no cast between object pointer
types, no union and no type punning, so no aliasing rule is stressed. `n` is initialized at its
declaration, so no uninitialized storage is read. The only arithmetic is that bounded increment and
a sum of four 0-or-1 operands, so no signed overflow is reachable. No object is modified twice
between sequence points.

CALLS. Every call passes a single argument, and no argument expression has any side effect at all,
so nothing depends on unspecified evaluation order. `printf` is hand-declared as
`int printf(const char *, ...);`, a prototype that matches every use: each call site supplies one
`%d` conversion specification and one argument of type `int`, several of them explicitly cast to
`int` from the `_Bool`-valued result of a comparison. No `%s` and no other conversion specification
appears anywhere in the program, so no string is interpolated into the output and no argument of any
other type reaches the variadic path.

THE ARCHITECTURE CONDITIONALS FALL BACK TO ZERO RATHER THAN DIAGNOSING. Each of the four
architecture blocks carries an alternative arm that defines a zero fallback instead of raising
`#error`. That choice is deliberate rather than lax. A diagnostic would mean that a compiler which
happens not to define the architecture macro spellings this program knows about fails to translate
the program at all, converting an informative output difference into an uninformative compile
failure on both oracles at once. With the zero fallback the program always compiles and always runs
under both compilers, and a macro gap surfaces, where it surfaces at all, as a comparable difference
with a precise diff rather than as a translation failure. What the fallback deliberately does NOT do
is make the gap itself an assertion: the program asserts no lower bound on the number of architecture
macros defined, for the reason set out in `impl_defined_notes`, so a compiler defining none of the
four satisfies every line here. No `#error` and no `#warning` appears on any path, so nothing is
written to standard error, which this suite captures into finding artifacts but never compares.

DETERMINISM. Every printed value is an `int` printed with `%d`, so nothing target-varying,
address-derived, time-derived, random or locale-dependent can reach standard output. No address and
no pointer value is printed. No plain `char` value is printed: `char` signedness was measured as
signed on x86_64 and i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64, so a plain-`char` value would diverge
for a reason that is not a defect. No raw type width is printed: `sizeof(long)` and `sizeof(void *)`
are 4 on i686 and 8 on the other three targets. No literal predefined-macro value is printed either,
which is the whole design of the program and is argued in `impl_defined_notes`. `__DATE__` and
`__TIME__` are never used anywhere in the source: they are timestamps, and a timestamp would make
byte-exact comparison impossible on the second run. `__FILE__` is used exactly once, inside a
non-emptiness relation, so its raw value -- an absolute or relative workspace path that differs from
cell to cell -- never reaches standard output; that was confirmed by building and running the
program from two directories with different absolute paths and observing byte-identical output.
`__LINE__` is likewise reduced to a positivity relation, so no literal line number is emitted and no
later edit to the comments above can change a printed value. Iteration order is fixed by the
terminator of a string literal. Output is a fixed eight-line sequence, one line per relation
claimed, so a single divergent line localizes a defect to one construct. `main` returns 0, inside
the 0-125 range the operating system delivers intact.

HERMETICITY. Every input is a literal in this source. Nothing is opened, nothing is read from the
environment, the command line, the clock or the file system, no socket is created, and no storage is
allocated, so a cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone and touches nothing
outside its own workspace.

NO HEADER IS INCLUDED, and that is why `printf` is declared by hand. bcc bundles only freestanding
headers and ships no hosted standard input/output header -- a search of the two authoritative
implementation documents, `docs/project-guide.md` and `docs/technical-specifications.md`, for `stdio`
returns no match, the claim being scoped to those two because the term does appear elsewhere under
`docs/`, in this suite's own methodology page `docs/testing/differential-conformance.md`, which
states this conclusion and therefore cannot be evidence for it. So naming a hosted header would fail
on the bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side: a spurious divergence caused by
the test rather than by a compiler.

GATE. The default warning gate applies unmodified and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears, because none
is needed: -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror. The program is
clean under that gate in the single native compile-only invocation the suite makes of it, and it
builds and runs clean in the one instrumented native build of -fsanitize=undefined,address
-fno-sanitize-recover=all, with output identical to the golden record below. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
THIS PROGRAM ASSERTS RELATIONS, NEVER LITERAL VALUES, AND THIS NOTE RECORDS WHY. It narrows nothing:
all four targets are swept, all three optimization levels are swept, all three oracles are enabled,
the default warning gate applies unmodified, and no expected-divergence marker is attached. What
follows is therefore not an excuse for a missing comparison. It is the record of how the comparison
was made comparable in the first place, and it is the reason this program discriminates instead of
diverging on every run.

WHICH MACROS MAY BE ASSERTED AS INVARIANTS, AND WHICH MAY NOT. This is a soundness requirement rather
than a stylistic preference. Only macros the C standard itself requires are invariants here:
`__STDC__` and `__STDC_VERSION__`, and the source-position macros `__LINE__` and `__FILE__`. A
conforming implementation must define each of them, so a divergence in one is a real conformance gap
and a legitimate finding.

ARCHITECTURE MACROS DIFFER PER TARGET BY DESIGN, AND ARE NOT INVARIANTS. `__x86_64__`, `__i386__`,
`__aarch64__` and `__riscv` are spellings of a particular compiler family. Printing any of them, or
printing a value derived directly from one, would guarantee a cross-backend difference that says
nothing whatever about compiler correctness, so the program prints normalized derived results
instead and never a macro name or a macro value. Two of them, and each is a property of a compiler's
consistency with ITSELF rather than a claim about what it must predefine: that NO MORE THAN ONE of
the four is defined (`arch_count_at_most_one`), because two simultaneous claims cannot both describe
the machine the code generator is emitting for; and that whichever one IS defined agrees with the
pointer width that generator actually produced (`arch_id_agrees_with_pointer_width`, written as a
two-sided implication so that it stays about agreement alone). Both lines are satisfied by a compiler
defining exactly one of the four, and both are satisfied by a compiler defining none. Only a compiler
that contradicts itself fails either, which is what makes a difference on these lines evidence about
the compiler rather than about a naming convention.

PRESENCE IS DELIBERATELY NOT ASSERTED, AND THIS IS THE RECORD OF THE WITHDRAWAL AND ITS REASON. An
earlier form of this program printed a third line, `arch_id_defined`, asserting that AT LEAST ONE of
the four spellings is defined, and this record carried `arch_id_defined=1` as golden output. The
observation that motivated it was correct: without such a line, a compiler predefining no
architecture macro produces output byte-identical to one predefining exactly the right macro, since
the sum is zero, zero is no more than one, and the implication is vacuously satisfied. The conclusion
drawn from it was not. Those two compilers agree because both are CORRECT. No clause of the standard
requires any of these four spellings; the search recorded in the next paragraph finds no repository
document that requires them of the compiler under test either; and this record itself conceded as
much while enforcing the opposite. An assertion no authority supports does not become sound by being
labelled a report: every one of this program's twelve cells would have reported a compiler which
spells its architecture macro otherwise, or which leaves the choice to a target header, as a
difference under all three oracles at once, and each of those differences would have been filed as an
undocumented FINDING. That is a false oracle, and a false oracle is worse than the blind spot it was
introduced to close, because it spends a maintainer's attention on permitted behaviour and teaches a
reader to distrust the finding set. Nor could such a difference have been reclassified as expected:
requirement 5 makes a marker's documented basis mandatory, and silence is not a basis.

WHAT THE WITHDRAWAL DOES NOT GIVE UP, since C3 forbids dropping a feature. All four architecture
macros are still read, all four conditional blocks are still exercised, both surviving relations are
still printed and compared, and this program still sweeps all four targets, all three optimization
levels and all three oracles: nothing is narrowed here, and no marker is attached. One unfounded
equality was withdrawn, not one line of coverage. The narrow alternative the review offered --
printing presence as capability metadata that no oracle compares -- is genuinely unavailable in this
suite rather than merely unattractive: comparison is byte-exact over the whole of standard output,
plus the raw wait status, so there is no uncompared channel a program can print into, and inventing
one would weaken the comparison for all 108 programs in order to describe one. What remains
observable about presence is observable where it belongs: the pre-flight capability report records
what each compiler is, and a maintainer curious about a compiler's predefined-macro set can read it
directly with that compiler's own dump-macros switch, which is a capability question rather than a
conformance one.

THE DOCUMENTATION GAP, AND WHY IT DECIDES THE DESIGN. The repository's implementation documentation
nowhere enumerates the macros any compiler predefines. A search of the two authoritative
implementation documents, `docs/project-guide.md` and `docs/technical-specifications.md`, for
`predefined`, `__STDC`, `__x86_64__`, `__i386__`, `__aarch64__`, `__riscv`, `__GNUC` and
`__STDC_HOSTED` returns no match for any of the eight spellings in either file. The claim is scoped
to those two rather than to `docs/` as a whole, and the reason is the same one the divergence register
gives for its own scoped searches: two of the eight spellings do occur elsewhere under `docs/`, in
this suite's own methodology page `docs/testing/differential-conformance.md`, which discusses this
very design decision and therefore cannot be evidence for it. There is consequently no documented
authority stating which predefined macros bcc defines or what values they take. That is
the direct reason this program asserts relations rather than literals, and it is the same reason the
presence assertion was withdrawn above: a relation is asserted here only where every correct compiler
must satisfy it. The gap has one further consequence. An expected-divergence marker requires a
documented basis, and a documented basis cannot be manufactured out of silence, so no marker could
legitimately be attached to this program even if a per-target difference were observed -- which is
precisely why the relations must be sound in the first place. A difference on a sound relation is
reported as a FINDING, and because the relations are normalized that finding is a precise, actionable
one rather than a wall of per-target noise nobody can triage.

LANGUAGE MODE AND THE ABSENCE OF A -std FLAG. bcc's documented command line
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 21 and 81) is -c, -o, -I, -D, -U, -L, -l, -g, -O0, -O1, -O2,
-shared, -fPIC, -mretpoline, -fcf-protection, -static and --target. There is no -std flag in it, so
no -std flag is ever passed in any differential invocation, on either side, and the reference
compiler therefore runs in its own default mode. That mode was measured rather than assumed:
`__STDC_VERSION__` is 201710L, `__STDC__` is 1, and `__STRICT_ANSI__` is absent -- gnu17, which
already offers the GNU extensions the corpus exercises elsewhere. Two of this program's eight
assertions rest on that measurement, so it is recorded here.

WHY THE STRICT-CONFORMANCE MACRO IS ASSERTED NOWHERE, IN EITHER DIRECTION. The measurement above
records that `__STRICT_ANSI__` is absent under the reference compiler, and bcc, having no -std flag,
can never be placed in a strict-ANSI mode either. It would therefore be tempting to assert its
absence as a relation expected to hold on both sides. That would be the wrong assertion, and for the
same reason the presence of an architecture spelling is not asserted either. `__STRICT_ANSI__` is a
compiler-family spelling that no clause
obliges an implementation to define or to omit, so a correct compiler is free to define it for
reasons of its own; requiring its absence would be a false oracle, and requiring its presence would
be another. An observation about one compiler's default mode is not a conformance requirement on
every compiler, and only relations that hold of any correct implementation are asserted here. Whether
GNU extensions are actually on offer is exercised where it belongs -- in feature area 08, by programs
that USE an extension -- rather than inferred here from the presence or absence of a macro.

THE STANDARD-VERSION ASSERTIONS ARE INEQUALITIES, NOT LITERALS: `__STDC_VERSION__ >= 199901L` and
`__STDC_VERSION__ >= 201112L`. The reference compiler reports 201710L, as measured above, and the
compiler under test is required to handle the full C11 standard rather than merely C99
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 758-762, the C11 and GCC Extensions Compliance Rule). Both
sides therefore satisfy both relations while neither is pinned to a particular edition, which is what
lets the two be compared at all: a literal assertion would have to name one edition and would fail
whichever side did not implement precisely that one, reporting an edition difference as a defect.

MACROS DELIBERATELY NOT EXAMINED, EACH FOR A STATED REASON. `__STDC_HOSTED__` is excluded because bcc
bundles only freestanding headers and ships no hosted input/output header, so it may legitimately
report 0 where the reference compiler reports 1; that is a hosted-versus-freestanding difference
rather than a preprocessing one, and only relations that hold under both compilers are asserted here.
`__GNUC__`, `__GNUC_MINOR__` and `__VERSION__` are excluded because whether bcc claims compatibility
with that compiler family through them is undocumented, so a difference would be uninformative -- and
because `__VERSION__` carries a version string that would differ between any two compilers and
between any two releases of one. `__DATE__` and `__TIME__` are excluded outright because they are
timestamps: byte-exact comparison against a golden record would fail on the second run by
construction. `__COUNTER__`, `__BASE_FILE__`, `__INCLUDE_LEVEL__`, the `__SIZEOF_*` family,
`__CHAR_BIT__` and `__INT_MAX__` are excluded for the same relations-only reason -- each either has no
standard mandate or carries a target-varying literal value, and printing one would manufacture a
difference rather than detect one. None of these exclusions removes a target, an optimization level
or an oracle from this program's matrix; each removes one macro spelling from the set of things
asserted about, and each is named here so the set not examined is as visible as the set that is.

WIDTH RELATIONS, AND WHY BOTH OF THEM ARE FOUR-TARGET INVARIANTS. Per the target table at
docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462, `x86_64-linux-gnu` has pointer 8 and `long` 8
(ELF64), `i686-linux-gnu` has pointer 4 and `long` 4 (ELF32), `aarch64-linux-gnu` has pointer 8 and
`long` 8 (ELF64), and `riscv64-linux-gnu` has pointer 8 and `long` 8 (ELF64). Pointer width therefore
equals `long` width on all four targets even though the shared value differs between the 32-bit
target and the other three, which makes `pointer_width_eq_long_width` a genuine invariant printed as
1 rather than a target-varying number. The line `arch_id_agrees_with_pointer_width` uses the same
table from the other direction, to tie the preprocessor's view of the target to the code generator's:
the 32-bit target is the only one of the four whose pointers are four bytes wide, so on it both sides
of the implication hold, and on the other three neither does. No raw width value is printed anywhere;
the one place a width literal appears at all is inside the relation `sizeof(void *) == 4u`, whose
truth value is combined with an architecture macro and never printed, and it is written unsigned so
that comparing it against the unsigned result of `sizeof` cannot trip a sign-comparison diagnostic
under the audit gate.

SOURCE-POSITION MACRO HANDLING. The raw value of `__FILE__` is never printed, because the path
differs per cell workspace and would break byte-exact comparison; only the path-independent relation
`slen(__FILE__) > 0` reaches the output. The raw value of `__LINE__` is never printed either, only its
positivity. The complementary technique -- substituting a virtual file name and line number with a
`#line` directive, which makes the source-position macros' literal values deterministic and therefore
directly comparable -- is not omitted from the corpus: it belongs to program 006 of this area, which
prints those substituted values outright.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
stdc_is_one=1
stdc_at_least_c99=1
stdc_at_least_c11=1
arch_count_at_most_one=1
arch_id_agrees_with_pointer_width=1
pointer_width_eq_long_width=1
line_macro_positive=1
file_macro_nonempty=1
END
